        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{\\frac{e}{5}}^{\\frac{e^{4}}{5}}\\frac{3}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}(5\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\ln\\left(5 \\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\right).$ Then  we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\u27f9\\,1\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{e}{5}$ | $\\frac{e^{4}}{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{\\frac{e}{5}}^{\\frac{e^{4}}{5}}\\frac{3}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}(5\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{6}{5}\\int_{\\frac{e}{5}}^{\\frac{e^{4}}{5}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}(5\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{6}{5}\\int_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{6}{5}\\int_{1}^{4}{u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(3\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{1/2}}{1/2}}\\right)|_{1}^{4} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(6\\cdot {\\sqrt{u}}\\right)|_{1}^{4} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(6(\\sqrt{4}-\\sqrt{1})\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(6\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
